From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:30:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: free the application's process before the kernel when
 loading fails

When the ROM or the system (the GPU, say) fails to load, Load shut the
kernel down and only then, returning, destroyed the Service::Process
holding the new KProcess: its finalization ran on the dead kernel (its
scheduler lock, slab heaps and page tables). glibc lets a destroyed mutex
be locked; the PS4's libc++ and pthreads don't ("mutex lock failed:
Invalid argument", then std::terminate), so a failed boot took the
emulator down instead of returning an error. The process is now freed
first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
---
 src/core/core.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/core.cpp b/src/core/core.cpp
index 046ee5334..c9aefcf02 100644
--- a/src/core/core.cpp
+++ b/src/core/core.cpp
@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@ struct System::Impl {
         auto process = Service::AM::CreateApplicationProcess(control, app_loader, load_result, system, file, params.program_id, params.program_index);
         if (load_result != Loader::ResultStatus::Success) {
             LOG_CRITICAL(Core, "Failed to load ROM (Error {})!", load_result);
+            process.reset(); // (its kernel process, before the kernel that owns it goes)
             ShutdownMainProcess();
             return SystemResultStatus(u32(SystemResultStatus::ErrorLoader) + u32(load_result));
         }
@@ -363,6 +364,7 @@ struct System::Impl {
         SystemResultStatus init_result{SetupForApplicationProcess(system, emu_window)};
         if (init_result != SystemResultStatus::Success) {
             LOG_CRITICAL(Core, "Failed to initialize system (Error {})!", int(init_result));
+            process.reset(); // (its kernel process, before the kernel that owns it goes)
             ShutdownMainProcess();
             return init_result;
         }
